{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSYzfQyeKUavAB12n1Ls","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class and create an OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method that:\n   - Throws 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Throws 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - If already CANCELLED, returns success (idempotent)\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments of the order\n   - Updates order status to CANCELLED and returns it\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Inject OrderRepository and check in the `create()` method whether the order is CANCELLED; if so, throw 409 Conflict.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: No new error codes needed; reuse existing ConflictException for:\n   - Confirmed shipment blocking cancel (409)\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order (409)\n   \n   Order not found uses existing ResourceNotFoundException (404).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Cancels an ACTIVE order and returns it\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotency)\n   - Cancelling an order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancelling a nonexistent order returns 404\n   - Cancelled shipments are visible after order cancellation\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test verifying that creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order fails with 409.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could have used a separate OrderService layer to encapsulate cancel logic, but the existing codebase has controllers directly using repositories and throwing exceptions, so staying consistent with existing patterns is better.\n- Could have added new error codes (e.g., ORDER_CANCELLED, CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS) but the ticket says \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" and doesn't specify unique codes for these cases, so reusing ConflictException is appropriate.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: Cancel an ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments*\n- Read: Find order by orderId (404 if not found), find all shipments for that order\n- Check: If any shipment is CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException (409, nothing changes)\n- Write: Update order status to CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n- Response: 200 OK with updated order\n\n*Case 2: Cancel an already CANCELLED order*\n- Read: Find order by orderId (404 if not found)\n- Check: Order already CANCELLED\n- Write: No writes\n- Response: 200 OK with the order (idempotent)\n\n*Case 3: Order doesn't exist*\n- Read: Try to find order\n- Response: 404 NOT_FOUND with error envelope\n\n*Case 4: Create shipment for CANCELLED order*\n- Read: Find order by orderId\n- Check: If order exists and is CANCELLED → throw ConflictException (409)\n- Response: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope (no shipment created)\n\n*Case 5: Create shipment for ACTIVE order (unchanged behavior)*\n- Existing behavior preserved\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest** new tests:\n   - `cancels_an_active_order_and_returns_200` - Create order (ACTIVE), cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED\n   - `cancel_an_active_order_with_created_shipments_cancels_those_shipments` - Create order and shipment, cancel order, verify shipment is CANCELLED\n   - `cancelling_an_already_cancelled_order_succeeds` - Create order, cancel twice, verify second cancel succeeds\n   - `cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` - Create order, create and confirm shipment, cancel returns 409, verify order still ACTIVE and shipment still CONFIRMED\n   - `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - Cancel non-existent order, verify 404 error\n   - `get_order_reports_cancelled_status` - Create order, cancel it, GET should show CANCELLED status\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest** new test:\n   - `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` - Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":19903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44e81e20-1948-495d-921e-89c02f6f0e07","uuid":"6b1ade2f-46e4-48fd-9411-642e55667fc8","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:50:02.756Z","request_id":"req_011CfSYzf39xnsVfcidiMrZf"}
