led order returns 409\" ✓\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** → Only code changes, no pom.xml modifications\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** → Only modified order and shipment features and api package as required\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `status: OrderStatus` field with default ACTIVE, added OrderStatus enum. Required because orders need state tracking.\n\n2. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId()` method to support finding shipments to cancel. Required for cancel operation.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt** - Added shipmentRepository injection and cancel endpoint with:\n   - 404 handling for missing orders\n   - Idempotency for already CANCELLED orders\n   - Conflict check for CONFIRMED shipments (409)\n   - Cascading cancellation of CREATED shipments\n   - Status update and persistence\n   \n   Required to implement the core cancel feature.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added orderRepository injection and check in create() to reject shipments for CANCELLED orders. Required to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Added two new error codes: `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` and `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED`. Required to provide descriptive error information.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 new test cases covering all cancellation scenarios including idempotency, conflict handling, error cases, and verification of cascading effects. Tests are required by acceptance criteria.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 1 new test case verifying shipment creation rejection for cancelled orders. Required by acceptance criteria.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All ticket requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint allowing customers to cancel orders until a carrier confirms a shipment, with idempotent retries and cascade cancellation of created shipments.\n\nChanged       Order.kt - Added status field and OrderStatus enum\n              ShipmentRepository.kt - Added findByOrderId() to support cancellation lookups\n              OrderController.kt - Added cancel() endpoint with full logic for all cases\n              ShipmentController.kt - Added cancelled order check to prevent shipment creation\n              ApiError.kt - Added error codes for cancelled and confirmed-shipment-blocked cases\n              OrderControllerTest.kt - Added 4 comprehensive test cases for cancel behavior\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Added test verifying shipment creation rejection for cancelled orders\n\nTests         newly created order has ACTIVE status - Verifies status initialization\n              cancels an active order and returns 200 - Core cancel functionality\n              cancel an active order with created shipments cancels those shipments - Cascade logic\n              cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds idempotently - Idempotency requirement\n              cancel with confirmed shipment returns 409 and changes nothing - Conflict atomicity\n              cancel nonexistent order returns 404 - Error handling\n              get order reports cancelled status - Status persistence\n              create shipment for cancelled order returns 409 - Prevention of shipments on cancelled orders\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service/)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - 21 tests passed (11 OrderControllerTest, 6 ShipmentControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, 3 CustomerControllerTest)\n\nNot done      None - all acceptance criteria satisfied\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3323,"cache_read_input_tokens":32485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3323},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"cont